---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
---

<StarlightPage
  frontmatter={{
    title: 'Privacy policy',
    description: 'WinConfig privacy policy',
  }}
  headings={[
    { depth: 2, slug: 'what-i-store', text: 'What I Store' },
    { depth: 2, slug: 'who-processes-it', text: 'Who Processes It' },
    { depth: 2, slug: 'how-long', text: 'How Long' },
    { depth: 2, slug: 'your-rights', text: 'Your Rights' },
  ]}
>
  <h2 id="what-i-store">What I Store</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Discord user ID (sign in with the <code>identify</code> scope only)
    </li>
    <li>Your PCs public key &amp; its PC moves</li>
    <li>
      Session data, means a hash of your sign in token, timestamps, and a coarse
      network value (first part of your IP address, your network operator &amp;
      country), I never store your full IP address
    </li>
    <li>Purchase data from Paddle</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The app sends no usage statistics or crash reports.</p>
  <h2 id="who-processes-it">Who Processes It</h2>
  <p>Cloudflare, Discord, Paddle</p>
  <h2 id="how-long">How Long</h2>
  <p>
    Account and license data as long as your account exists, sessions end after
    90 days unused, security logs and PC move history are deleted after 90 days,
    and transaction records are kept as tax law requires.
  </p>
  <h2 id="your-rights">Your Rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask for access, correction, deletion, restriction or a copy of your
    data, and object to the processing on the basis of a legitimate interest
    (contact@noverse.dev).
  </p>
</StarlightPage>
